# These fixtures are terminal-capture data: the exact bytes ARE the test input.
#
# CR is load-bearing. In a terminal, LF moves the cursor DOWN but does not
# return it to column 0 — that is what CR does. A fixture written with bare LF
# therefore produces progressively indented rows in the emulator, which is not
# what a real PTY stream looks like and changes how lines classify. (That is
# exactly how 06-response came to fail: its second line landed at column 34, so
# the user-input `> ` check, which is anchored at line start, never matched.)
#
# Marking them -text disables all line-ending normalisation, so a checkout on a
# machine with core.autocrlf=true cannot silently rewrite them.
*.txt -text
*.raw -text
